      "rationale": "This rule defines the named ascending predicate by expanding it to list equality against the recursively defined ascending sort; it is a mathematical summary equation, not a separately established fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-f99627839f69163b45f7724548ffd1e71c6f80dfb7bdbd7578083347002cc84e",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule ascending(IS) => eqIntLists(IS, sortInts(IS))"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 13,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "3b19f7a8e59183f961c42635af0892ad86d88a1503a978ee2d19b6ebbbbfbe18",
      "rationale": "This rule defines duplicateBound as the existing at-most-two counting summary applied to the same input list in both roles; it is a direct named-predicate expansion.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-3b19f7a8e59183f961c42635af0892ad86d88a1503a978ee2d19b6ebbbbfbe18",
      "start_line": 13,
      "text": "  rule duplicateBound(IS) => countsAtMostTwo(IS, IS)"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 16,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "15283af6a5fb0ffd622a25de42f40dce807a8a9fa5cc8d22f978f38853963a27",
      "rationale": "This rule defines isSortedContract as the conjunction of the two previously named contract components, so it is a macro-style contract aggregation.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-15283af6a5fb0ffd622a25de42f40dce807a8a9fa5cc8d22f978f38853963a27",
      "start_line": 16,
      "text": "  rule isSortedContract(IS) => ascending(IS) andBool duplicateBound(IS)"
    }
  ],
